Fields that can be used: **/basic/siteName, /basic/subMerchantId**
Operations that can be used: **replace, remove**
Sample request: 

    [
       {
           "value": "MySite",
           "path": "/basic/siteName",
           "op": "replace"             
       }, 
       {
           "value": "123456",
           "path": "/basic/subMerchantId",
           "op": "replace"             
       }
    ]

Fields that can be used: **/addresses/0/streetName, /addresses/0/houseNumber**
Operations that can be used: **replace, remove**
Sample request: 

    [
       {
           "value": "Mainstreet",
           "path": "/addresses/0/streetName",
           "op": "replace"             
       }, 
       {
           "value": 12,
           "path": "/addresses/0/houseNumber",
           "op": "replace"             
       }
    ]

Based on a GET Site Addresses call a PATCH Site Addresses call can be generated to change one or more fields. Whether it is allowed to change a field (and which values are allowed) is determined by the business logic of the contract management solution. Since a site only has one address the index is always 0
